From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] do not enable xtensor's xsimd backend on riscv64

cmake/xtensor.cmake unconditionally defines XTENSOR_USE_XSIMD (and sets
the xtensor CMake option of the same name, which xtensor's interface
target also propagates as a compile definition). xtensor then allocates
every xarray buffer through xsimd::aligned_allocator<T,
XSIMD_DEFAULT_ALIGNMENT>.

The pinned xsimd 7.4.10 only knows x86 and ARM instruction sets. On
riscv64 it detects none ("No SIMD instructions set detected" #warning)
and, with GCC >= 7, defines XSIMD_DEFAULT_ALIGNMENT to 0.
detail::xaligned_malloc() returns nullptr whenever the alignment is 0,
so aligned_allocator::allocate() throws std::bad_alloc on every
allocation: every TensorStorage, and therefore every PlainTensor,
CKKSTensor and BFVTensor, fails to construct, e.g.

    ts.plain_tensor([0])  ->  MemoryError: std::bad_alloc

Reproduced with a standalone program building
xt::xarray<double>(xt::adapt(vector, shape)) against xtl 0.7.2, xsimd
7.4.10 and xtensor 0.23.5 under GCC 14 in manylinux_2_39_riscv64: it
throws std::bad_alloc with -DXTENSOR_USE_XSIMD and works without it.

TenSEAL never uses xsimd directly, so on riscv64 leave XTENSOR_USE_XSIMD
off and let xtensor use std::allocator with its scalar code paths.
xsimd is still fetched and on the include path, so LICENSE.xsimd stays
in the wheel.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 cmake/xtensor.cmake | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cmake/xtensor.cmake b/cmake/xtensor.cmake
index fe48ee0..281ae89 100644
--- a/cmake/xtensor.cmake
+++ b/cmake/xtensor.cmake
@@ -1,7 +1,11 @@
 include(FetchContent)
 
-add_definitions(-DXTENSOR_USE_XSIMD)
-set(XTENSOR_USE_XSIMD ON)
+# xsimd 7.x has no RISC-V backend: XSIMD_DEFAULT_ALIGNMENT is 0 there and
+# xsimd::aligned_allocator then throws std::bad_alloc on every allocation.
+if(NOT CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "^riscv")
+  add_definitions(-DXTENSOR_USE_XSIMD)
+  set(XTENSOR_USE_XSIMD ON)
+endif()
 set(JSON_BuildTests OFF)
 set(JSON_Install OFF)
 
